              "message": "Templates: four short trailers on a governed commit, and signing that follows the committer\n\nA governed commit now says who drafted it, who reviewed it, who signed it\noff and which approval it carries, and nothing more. Drafted-by names the\nmodel, Reviewed-by each approving reviewer by name and email,\nSigned-off-by the committer, and CHAP-Approval the task whose evidence\nthe note holds, with the commit's place in an approved branch. The\nworkspace, the gate's address, the keys, the decision, the rule and the\nchain head stay in the note, where the verifier reads them. Commits in the\nlonger form an earlier version wrote still verify.\n\nThe gate's commits are signed as the committer signs their own\n(sign_commits: committer, the default), so a code host shows them like the\ncommitter's other commits; sign_commits: agent keeps signing with the\nagent's key. A git signature is checked against the keys the trust policy\nlists and fails a commit only where signed commits are required, and the\npull request workflow leaves that requirement for a team to switch on.",
