              "message": "Templates: one command runs the review loop, and each decision comes back to the agent as a prompt\n\npropose.mjs and propose-branch.mjs start the gate in the background when\nnone runs on the machine, bring the review to the reviewer (an open desk\nshows it, and the browser opens otherwise), and wait within the time an\nagent's tool call allows: with --timeout, exit code 4 says to run the same\ncommand again. npm run stop stops a gate started this way.\n\nEach decision becomes a prompt for the agent, printed by the command and\nshown in the desk with a Copy button: the reviewer's note, their comments\non lines with the code each is about, an edit as a diff, and the command\nto run again. Exit code 3 asks for changes, and 2 is a rejection.\n\nThe agent's context note (--context) travels with the proposal and sits\nabove the change in the desk, and a revision carries what changed since\nthe reviewer last looked. The desk shows the code around a change where\nthe file's text came with it, comments on lines go with the decision onto\nthe chain, and the desk's typography is reworked for long reviews.",
