              "message": "Templates: the desk's text grows with the window, and each reviewer can make it larger\n\nThe desk's root size follows the width of the window, from 16px on a phone\nor a small laptop to 20px on a large monitor, starting from the browser's\nown text size setting, and every size in the desk is relative to it. Two\nbuttons at the top make the text smaller or larger, and the browser keeps\nthe choice for next time.\n\nOn a phone the bar at the top takes two lines, the queue a smaller part of\nthe screen and the decision buttons one row, and on a touch screen the\nbutton to comment on a line shows on every line. The bar gives way to a\nnarrow window by shortening the profiles first, and names the reviewer\nwithout their URI unless two share a name. The days under the Insights\nchart are text, so they keep their size, and a wide table scrolls inside\nits card.",
